problem:
A sequence of numbers \(a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots\) is defined recursively by \(a_1 = 1\) and for \(n > 1\),
\[a_n = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
a_{n-1} + 3 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd}, \\
a_{n-1}^2 - 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]
Find the remainder when \(a_{2023}\) is divided by 7.

Let $ABC$ be an acute-angled triangle with circumradius $R$. Points $D$ and $E$ lie on sides $AB$ and $AC$, respectively, such that $AD = DE = EC = R$. If $M$ is the midpoint of $BC$, determine the maximum possible value of the area of triangle $ADE$.

