Find the smallest positive integer $k$ such that $a_k = a_1$.

Find all positive integers \( n \) such that the equation \[
x^n + y^n + z^n = x^{n+1} + y^{n+1} + z^{n+1}
\] has a solution in positive integers \( x, y, \) and \( z \) with \( x, y, z \) not all equal.

Determine the number of ordered pairs of positive integers (x, y) that satisfy the following system of equations:
\[
\begin{cases}
x^4 - 4y^4 = 4x^2 - y^4 \\
x + y = 2023
\end{cases}

In a sequence of numbers \( a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots, a_{2023} \), each term is determined by the following rule:
\[ a_{n+1} = \begin{cases} 
a_n + 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is even} \\
a_n - 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is odd} 
\end{cases} \]
Given that \( a_1 = 1 \), what is the smallest positive integer \( k \) such that \( a_k = a_{k+1} \)?

Consider a sequence of positive integers \(a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots, a_{100}\) such that for every \(i\) from 1 to 99, the following holds:
\[ a_{i+1} = \begin{cases} 
a_i + 1 & \text{if } a_i \text{ is odd} \\
a_i / 2 & \text{if } a_i \text{ is even}
\end{cases} \]
Given that \(a_{100} = 1\), determine the number of possible values for \(a_1\).
